            <ArticleTitle>A review of reflex sympathetic dystrophy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1651-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reflex sympathetic dystrophy, or as it is now known, complex regional pain syndrome, Type 1, is an unusual complication of a variety of injuries whose development should be suspected in the presence of disproportionate pain coupled with autonomic disturbance. Early recognition and treatment with multimodality therapy offer a high probability of recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
